    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "WHERE AM I",
      "narration_text": "First, where are you. Your phone times signals from at least four satellites. Three pin down where you are, and the fourth corrects your phone's clock, which matters: one millisecond off is three hundred kilometres. In my simulation, open sky gave about five metres. Between tall buildings, about seventy. That's the blue circle: how unsure it is.",
