    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "THE ROUTE",
      "narration_text": "To find a route, the roads become a graph: corners joined by streets, each with a travel time. I built a city with nine hundred corners. Dijkstra's algorithm checked eight hundred and twenty-six of them. A-star, which aims at the destination, checked five hundred and forty-seven, and found the same route. Google doesn't publish its exact recipe.",
