    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "TRAFFIC",
      "narration_text": "Traffic comes from phones. Since two thousand nine, phones with location on have sent anonymous speeds, compared with how each road usually behaves. In my city, history alone coloured eighty-seven percent of roads right, but missed a crash. Five hundred phones were enough to turn it red.",
